<title>ZIMBABWE: Salim gets third four-term as OAU chief.</title>
<headline>Salim gets third four-term as OAU chief.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salim Ahmed Salim was re-elected on Monday to a third four-year term as secretary-general of the Organisation of African Unity at an OAU summit in Zimbabwe.</p>
<p>The Tanzanian diplomat was the only candidate after the withdrawal last Saturday of Ivory Coast's Foreign Minister Amara Essy who said he did want to divide Africa on the issue.</p>
<p>OAU spokesman Ibrahim Dagash said Salim got the backing of 37 of the 47 members who voted. Five members were not eligible to vote because they have huge arrears on their membership fees.</p>
<p>Salim, 55, needed the support of two-thirds of the voting members to retain the job.</p>
</text>
